    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1312">

                <pb facs="1134" n="820" xml:id="pg820"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/69</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires’ in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-12-04">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>345. Your 275, 17th. Foreign Office apparently unwilling to give definite answer
                    at this time but states that it does not anticipate any trouble will be
                    encountered from French authorities or representatives by American committee in
                    sending supplies to destitute Belgians in Belgium.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bliss</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
